WEBVTT

NOTE LUMO, The Gospel of Luke 12:1-59 (Arclight 6_GOLuke2613), en.
NOTE Timings: whisper.cpp small -dtw small per speech burst on the isolated dialogue (dialoguenhance centre channel), first word on the burst start, 2026-11-11.

1
00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:24.450
Be dressed ready for service, and keep your lamps burning,

2
00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.800
like servants waiting for their master to return

3
00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:31.900
from a wedding banquet, so that when he comes and knocks,

4
00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.900
they can immediately open the door for him.

5
00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:36.650
It will be good for those servants

6
00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:39.710
whose master finds them watching when he comes.

7
00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:43.960
Truly I tell you, he will dress himself to serve,

8
00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:45.950
will have them recline at the table,

9
00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:49.110
and will come and wait on them.

10
00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:53.290
It will be good for those servants whose master finds them ready,

11
00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:55.030
even if he comes in the middle of the night

12
00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:57.600
or toward daybreak.

13
00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.740
But understand this: if the owner of the house

14
00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.950
had known at what hour the thief was coming,

15
00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:07.350
he would not have let his house be broken into.

16
00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.180
You also must be ready, because the Son of Man

17
00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.700
will come at an hour when you do not expect him.
